UML Exception Tree - Lab 5
============================

Java Exception Hierarchy:
-------------------------

Throwable
├── Error
│   ├── OutOfMemoryError
│   ├── StackOverflowError
│   └── VirtualMachineError
└── Exception
    ├── RuntimeException
    │   ├── NullPointerException
    │   ├── IllegalArgumentException
    │   ├── NumberFormatException
    │   └── IndexOutOfBoundsException
    ├── IOException
    │   ├── FileNotFoundException
    │   └── EOFException
    ├── ClassNotFoundException
    └── Custom Exceptions
        └── PlayerException (AIMS Custom)

AIMS Project Exception Handling:
-------------------------------

PlayerException (Custom)
├── Purpose: Handle media playback errors
├── Thrown by:
│   ├── DigitalVideoDisc.play()
│   ├── CompactDisc.play()
│   └── Track.play()
├── Usage in Controllers:
│   ├── MediaItemController.play()
│   ├── CartController.playMedia()
│   └── Aims.main()
└── Error Scenarios:
    ├── DVD length <= 0
    ├── CD total length <= 0
    └── Track length <= 0

Exception Flow in AIMS:
------------------------

1. Media.play() methods
   ├── Check validation (length > 0)
   ├── if invalid → throw PlayerException
   └── if valid → proceed with playback

2. Controller methods
   ├── try-catch PlayerException
   ├── Show error dialog (JavaFX Alert)
   └── Log error to console

3. Main application
   ├── try-catch for initialization
   ├── Handle FXML loading errors
   └── Graceful error recovery

Exception Handling Patterns:
---------------------------

1. Validation Pattern:
   ```java
   if (getLength() <= 0) {
       throw new PlayerException("Invalid length: " + getLength());
   }
   ```

2. Try-Catch Pattern:
   ```java
   try {
       ((Playable) media).play();
   } catch (PlayerException e) {
       showAlert("Play Error", e.getMessage(), Alert.AlertType.ERROR);
   }
   ```

3. Exception Propagation:
   ```java
   public void play() throws PlayerException {
       // CD level
       for (Track t : tracks) {
           try {
               t.play();
           } catch (PlayerException e) {
               throw e; // Re-throw to caller
           }
       }
   }
   ```

Best Practices Implemented:
---------------------------

✅ Custom exception for domain-specific errors
✅ Proper exception messages with context
✅ Exception chaining (cause preservation)
✅ Try-catch at UI layer for user feedback
✅ Validation before throwing exceptions
✅ Exception propagation where appropriate
✅ User-friendly error dialogs
✅ Console logging for debugging

